1
00:00:05,617 --> 00:00:13,543
[SPEAKER_00]: This is an anicca saṃpāya sūtan, suitable for the imperturbable.

2
00:00:13,603 --> 00:00:15,324
[SPEAKER_00]: Majjhmanikā 106.

3
00:00:17,926 --> 00:00:18,866
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus have I heard.

4
00:00:19,507 --> 00:00:24,931
[SPEAKER_00]: On one occasion, the Buddha was living among the Kurus, in a town of the Kurus called Kamasatama.

5
00:00:27,552 --> 00:00:29,234
[SPEAKER_00]: There, the Blessed One addressed the bhikkhus.

6
00:00:31,095 --> 00:00:31,515
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhikkhus?

7
00:00:31,855 --> 00:00:32,396
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, Bhante.

8
00:00:32,716 --> 00:00:33,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Those bhikkhus replied.

9
00:00:34,197 --> 00:00:35,198
[SPEAKER_00]: The Blessed One said this.

10
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:42,383
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, sense-desires are impermanent, empty, false, deceptive.

11
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:47,706
[SPEAKER_00]: That which is fraudulent, because, is the utterance of a fool.

12
00:00:49,047 --> 00:01:00,874
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, whatever sense-desires here and now, and whatever sense-desires in lives to come, whatever perceptions of sense-desires here and now, and whatever perceptions of sense-desires in lives to come,

13
00:01:01,462 --> 00:01:06,784
[SPEAKER_00]: Both of these are māras realm, māras province, māras bait, māras feeding ground.

14
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:28,711
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the thing to note here is that whatever sense desires here and now, and whatever sense desires in lives to come, means whatever sense desires are present, and whatever possibilities of sense desires are also present, right here, right now, as possibilities.

15
00:01:29,311 --> 00:01:30,852
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the important thing to discern.

16
00:01:32,727 --> 00:01:48,891
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, eh... seeing, for example, an arisen sensual desire, right here, right now, and overcoming it on that basis, through thinking about non-attractive or how dangerous it is and so on, that's all fine.

17
00:01:49,051 --> 00:01:57,993
[SPEAKER_00]: But what one person also needs to see is the simultaneously present possibilities of sensuality for the future.

18
00:01:59,343 --> 00:02:10,951
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you might deal with a particular arising of sensual desire, but you also want to deal with what's peripheral to that particular arising, which is possibilities for more arising.

19
00:02:11,332 --> 00:02:12,873
[SPEAKER_00]: Not now, later.

20
00:02:13,273 --> 00:02:28,044
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even if you overcome a particular sensual desire that has arisen, you want to, eh... you don't want to rest, so to speak, in that overcoming, but you want to see that the possibilities of these things being manifested again,

21
00:02:30,866 --> 00:02:40,409
[SPEAKER_00]: Tomorrow, in the next day, and in two years, in ten years, in ten lifetimes, you want to see that that's still present, and above all, it's still applicable to you.

22
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:52,433
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why the one who reflects rightly, needs to include it in the reflection, that not just the present sensuality, it's, eh...

23
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,354
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impermanent, empty, false, deceptive.

24
00:02:56,034 --> 00:02:57,054
[SPEAKER_00]: It should be unwanted.

25
00:02:57,575 --> 00:03:02,557
[SPEAKER_00]: But also, that liability to future sensuality as well should be seen the same.

26
00:03:02,777 --> 00:03:10,620
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how you truly surmount the entire domain, not just a particular manifestation of it.

27
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:17,362
[SPEAKER_00]: It says further, here these evil unwholesome things lead to mental covetousness, ill will and anger.

28
00:03:18,483 --> 00:03:21,524
[SPEAKER_00]: They create an obstacle for a noble disciple in training here.

29
00:03:23,013 --> 00:03:27,836
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they create an obstacle for somebody who has the right view, at least.

30
00:03:28,036 --> 00:03:30,998
[SPEAKER_00]: And yes, that's... it's said in other suttas as well.

31
00:03:32,239 --> 00:03:46,728
[SPEAKER_00]: A noble disciple, sotāpanna or higher, will... could be... no, it's not a guarantee, but he could be distracted still with sensuality, with sense desires, by not fully dwelling on the danger of it.

32
00:03:49,297 --> 00:03:53,440
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it says, in this case, a bhikkhu, a noble disciple, reflects thus.

33
00:03:53,480 --> 00:04:02,728
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever sense desire here and now, whatever sense desires in lives to come, whatever perceptions of sense desires here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires in lives to come.

34
00:04:03,228 --> 00:04:07,832
[SPEAKER_00]: And again, this is if anybody wonders whether it it means as a possibility future, it does.

35
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:09,573
[SPEAKER_00]: Because how could you be perceiving

36
00:04:10,654 --> 00:04:14,056
[SPEAKER_00]: Sense desires in lives to come when those lives aren't there.

37
00:04:14,356 --> 00:04:15,297
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole point.

38
00:04:15,557 --> 00:04:21,221
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't want to wait for the every manifestation of sensuality to arise and affect you.

39
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:23,422
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to see it on the level of possibility.

40
00:04:24,343 --> 00:04:31,608
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is the peripheral level in regard to the actually, currently, particularly present sensuality and sensual domain.

41
00:04:32,636 --> 00:04:43,165
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whatever perceptions of these possibilities you have, as in, whatever perceptions of sense desires and lives to come, you want to see that as well as pertaining to the perceptions of sensuality here and now.

42
00:04:47,329 --> 00:04:52,173
[SPEAKER_00]: So, both of these things are māras realm, māras province, māras bait, māras feeding ground.

43
00:04:53,527 --> 00:04:58,070
[SPEAKER_00]: And here, these evil unwholesome things lead to mental covetousness, ill will and anger.

44
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,812
[SPEAKER_00]: They create an obstacle for a noble disciple in training here.

45
00:05:01,653 --> 00:05:06,616
[SPEAKER_00]: What if I were to dwell with a mind that is large, expanded, having mentally determined to surmount the world?

46
00:05:07,437 --> 00:05:14,501
[SPEAKER_00]: And again, this is not a... we spoke about this before in the in the few talks on meditation, how to establish your mind.

47
00:05:15,422 --> 00:05:16,543
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's exactly what this is.

48
00:05:18,917 --> 00:05:36,161
[SPEAKER_00]: Expanded mind, so to speak, means mind that has overcome through including the discernment of both particular sensuality and the domain of the peripherally possible sensual experience.

49
00:05:36,721 --> 00:05:38,442
[SPEAKER_00]: So, without a particular manifestation.

50
00:05:38,802 --> 00:05:42,263
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you go truly beyond the entire domain of sensuality, as I just said.

51
00:05:43,308 --> 00:05:46,530
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the mind then gets expanded beyond it, so to speak, large.

52
00:05:47,151 --> 00:05:53,335
[SPEAKER_00]: Having mentally determined to surmount the world, which is what sensuality is for somebody who is still bound with sensual desire.

53
00:05:55,222 --> 00:06:03,826
[SPEAKER_00]: So, surmounting, expanding, establishing your mind above it, enlarging it, whatever words you use, that's the point.

54
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:17,192
[SPEAKER_00]: Not just overcoming one particular perception of sensuality that is currently arisen and enduring for you, but you want to start discerning possibilities of being affected by sensuality in the future.

55
00:06:17,672 --> 00:06:23,075
[SPEAKER_00]: That also partakes in the domain of particularly present enduring sensuality for you.

56
00:06:24,352 --> 00:06:30,575
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same manner then, when there is no particular manifestation of some sensual desire, you could review your mind and see.

57
00:06:31,075 --> 00:06:37,779
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so maybe there is no particular manifestation of sensuality that's bothering me now, but would that be true for the future?

58
00:06:38,779 --> 00:06:45,542
[SPEAKER_00]: Will in the future, when the sensual objects manifest themselves, will I also remain unbothered by it?

59
00:06:46,043 --> 00:06:52,586
[SPEAKER_00]: If the answer is no, means the mind hasn't been large and large expanded and mentally determined to surmount the world.

60
00:06:54,234 --> 00:07:01,221
[SPEAKER_00]: So, for somebody with the right view, they realize they only need to do is maintain the establishment of the mind on that expanded level.

61
00:07:01,741 --> 00:07:12,232
[SPEAKER_00]: Expanded is a relative sense, of course, but expanded in a sense of surmounting and having included both particular sensuality and possibilities of sensualities in the lives to come.

62
00:07:13,353 --> 00:07:17,177
[SPEAKER_00]: Include it and just don't descend down on that level.

63
00:07:18,892 --> 00:07:28,174
[SPEAKER_00]: Because dwelling with the mind that is large, expanded, having mentally determined to surmount the world, there will be none of this evil, unwholesome, mental covetousness, ill-will and anger.

64
00:07:28,755 --> 00:07:33,916
[SPEAKER_00]: Because mental covetousness, ill-will and anger need the sensual domain as its basis.

65
00:07:34,916 --> 00:07:38,057
[SPEAKER_00]: Having surmounted the entire sensual domain correctly,

66
00:07:38,683 --> 00:07:40,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means you're not contacted by it.

67
00:07:40,944 --> 00:07:45,285
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, ill-will, covetousness and anger cannot affect you either.

68
00:07:45,325 --> 00:07:46,546
[SPEAKER_00]: They cannot manifest.

69
00:07:47,346 --> 00:07:54,088
[SPEAKER_00]: Having abandoned these, the Noble Disciple reflects further, my mind will be unlimited, unbounded and well-developed.

70
00:07:54,448 --> 00:07:56,609
[SPEAKER_00]: That's exactly... that's exactly what we just described.

71
00:07:56,649 --> 00:08:05,352
[SPEAKER_00]: Large, expanded and so on, means unlimited by essentiality, unbounded, uncontrolled, not liable to it, well-developed.

72
00:08:07,441 --> 00:08:11,844
[SPEAKER_00]: Having practiced this way, having often dwelled like this, his mind develops clarity in this domain.

73
00:08:12,845 --> 00:08:13,825
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's another thing.

74
00:08:13,865 --> 00:08:17,648
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the mind gets established upon these right type of thoughts.

75
00:08:18,208 --> 00:08:23,372
[SPEAKER_00]: Thoughts of the sensual domain correctly, not misconceiving it, not ignoring it, not not seeing it.

76
00:08:24,152 --> 00:08:26,594
[SPEAKER_00]: Thoughts of liability to future sensuality.

77
00:08:27,394 --> 00:08:30,797
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when the mind is properly established, then the monk dwells.

78
00:08:31,477 --> 00:08:32,157
[SPEAKER_00]: in that state.

79
00:08:32,437 --> 00:08:36,238
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, it's not a meditative experience where he's frozen into.

80
00:08:36,778 --> 00:08:51,421
[SPEAKER_00]: Means the mind has reflected correctly, surmounted things that need to be surmounted, keeps a watchful eye on greed, aversion, delusion to not manifest, because that would mean he has gone back into that domain where these things manifest.

81
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:55,522
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he goes around his day dwelling in this state.

82
00:08:56,222 --> 00:08:57,383
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what... that's exactly what it means.

83
00:08:57,443 --> 00:08:59,083
[SPEAKER_00]: Having often dwelled like this.

84
00:09:00,385 --> 00:09:01,906
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he spends time in it.

85
00:09:02,946 --> 00:09:04,887
[SPEAKER_00]: His minds develop clarity in this domain.

86
00:09:06,548 --> 00:09:13,011
[SPEAKER_00]: With clarity, either he enters upon the imperturbable now, or he inclines towards it with understanding.

87
00:09:13,271 --> 00:09:15,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, clarity of what imperturbable is.

88
00:09:16,213 --> 00:09:19,134
[SPEAKER_00]: Understanding of what imperturbable is.

89
00:09:19,795 --> 00:09:22,116
[SPEAKER_00]: That's, that's, eh... that's how he enters it.

90
00:09:22,376 --> 00:09:23,417
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how he develops it.

91
00:09:23,577 --> 00:09:25,918
[SPEAKER_00]: Imperturbable means imperturbable by sensuality.

92
00:09:26,718 --> 00:09:29,880
[SPEAKER_00]: Means the possibility of sensual domain cannot, eh...

93
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:36,826
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't distract one anymore, because he dwelled long enough away from it.

94
00:09:36,886 --> 00:09:47,137
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, on the breakup of the body, after death, it is possible that consciousness that has been involved with this will reach the imperturbable.

95
00:09:52,198 --> 00:09:59,881
[SPEAKER_00]: That means that consciousness that has been involved with this means he's been making these phenomena endure presently for him.

96
00:09:59,961 --> 00:10:02,421
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, somebody can just think about imperturbable.

97
00:10:03,622 --> 00:10:04,282
[SPEAKER_00]: That's one thing.

98
00:10:04,362 --> 00:10:09,984
[SPEAKER_00]: But another thing is to think rightly about the imperturbable domain, develop understanding and then dwell in it.

99
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:13,782
[SPEAKER_00]: By dwelling in it, that domain is present for you.

100
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:16,023
[SPEAKER_00]: Whenever there is presence, that's what consciousness is.

101
00:10:16,704 --> 00:10:29,991
[SPEAKER_00]: So, through often dwelling in such a phenomenon of the imperturbable domain that has surmounted sensuality, his consciousness has been involved with this sufficiently.

102
00:10:30,372 --> 00:10:37,516
[SPEAKER_00]: And because of that, in the moment, well, after death, it could reach the imperturbable.

103
00:10:40,227 --> 00:10:42,387
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the first way suitable for the imperturbable.

104
00:10:43,488 --> 00:10:47,028
[SPEAKER_00]: The second way is noble disciple reflects thus.

105
00:10:47,528 --> 00:11:08,192
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever sense desires here and now, whatever sense desires in lives to come, whatever perceptions of sense desires here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires in lives to come, whatever matter, all matter is the four great elements and from the four great elements matter is assumed, matter is held up, matter is misconceived or conceived, just that.

106
00:11:09,117 --> 00:11:13,339
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when he practices in this way, having often dwelt like this, his mind develops clarity in this domain.

107
00:11:13,379 --> 00:11:17,882
[SPEAKER_00]: With clarity, he enters upon the imperturbable, or he inclines towards it with understanding.

108
00:11:17,902 --> 00:11:24,625
[SPEAKER_00]: On the breakup of the body after death, it is possible that the consciousness involved with this will reach the imperturbable.

109
00:11:24,745 --> 00:11:25,565
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the second way.

110
00:11:26,786 --> 00:11:38,232
[SPEAKER_00]: So, here, one might wonder, eh, why does Buddha talk about sensuality, sensual desires in lives to come, da-da-da, and then, all matter is the four great elements, and from the four great elements, matter is assumed.

111
00:11:40,093 --> 00:11:41,273
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, where's the connection there?

112
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:56,679
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the connection there is... Can you even think about any central object of any sense, if there is no... an actual, factual, material presence, existence of that thing?

113
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:01,061
[SPEAKER_00]: If there is no matter to be assumed,

114
00:12:03,297 --> 00:12:07,141
[SPEAKER_00]: How can there be attraction to a material form of any kind?

115
00:12:07,221 --> 00:12:09,183
[SPEAKER_00]: How can there be lust towards it?

116
00:12:09,844 --> 00:12:21,616
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the heart of any and every sensuality, here and now, in the heart of every possibility of sensuality for the lives to come, one thing that's universally in common,

117
00:12:22,568 --> 00:12:36,411
[SPEAKER_00]: is that independence of four great elements, independence of material aspect, which means anything sensual, any sensual object is completely circumstantial, accidental, you could even say.

118
00:12:37,371 --> 00:12:47,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Not that your sensuality and your sensual preferences and proliferation is accidental, but the material aspect of every sensual object could have not been.

119
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:50,153
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally.

120
00:12:51,535 --> 00:12:53,277
[SPEAKER_00]: It is, but it could have not been.

121
00:12:54,358 --> 00:12:55,279
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole point.

122
00:12:57,161 --> 00:12:58,683
[SPEAKER_00]: Four great elements.

123
00:12:58,763 --> 00:13:06,532
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, they're so great, you can't even appropriate them, let alone have them and regard them as yours, and have them obey your will, and so on.

124
00:13:07,425 --> 00:13:17,870
[SPEAKER_00]: So... and that's... that's in... like, even if you possess the sensual object in its heart, the material, the materiality of the sensual object is something utterly inaccessible to you.

125
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:24,933
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can apply the same to your own body, to the body of others, to the sense objects, to your own senses.

126
00:13:24,993 --> 00:13:26,774
[SPEAKER_00]: It's... it's utterly enclosed.

127
00:13:26,894 --> 00:13:31,856
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the entire sensual domain is utterly enclosed within the material domain.

128
00:13:33,437 --> 00:13:36,438
[SPEAKER_00]: And as such, it's... it's... it's inaccessible.

129
00:13:37,682 --> 00:13:43,905
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just you cannot even conceive how to come underneath, so to speak, and truly own it.

130
00:13:44,385 --> 00:13:58,931
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can only entertain the notion of ownership through gratuitously taking for granted the offered careless pleasure in regard to it, the pleasure, the distraction.

131
00:14:00,075 --> 00:14:16,059
[SPEAKER_00]: That you get through satisfying that possibility of pleasure on that surface, but that cannot uphold, then, pick up that whole sensual domain and make it yours, despite what the sensuality tells you.

132
00:14:16,099 --> 00:14:17,559
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why the Buddha said it's a fraud.

133
00:14:18,219 --> 00:14:18,899
[SPEAKER_00]: It deceives you.

134
00:14:18,959 --> 00:14:19,520
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a bait.

135
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:29,282
[SPEAKER_00]: You jump on it thinking, I'll have this failing to see that it contains a hook that actually hooks you up and baits you like a fish.

136
00:14:34,125 --> 00:14:37,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he says, furthermore, because a noble disciple reflects thus.

137
00:14:38,268 --> 00:14:55,923
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever sense desires here and now, whatever sense desires in lives to come, whatever perceptions of sense desires here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires in lives to come, whatever matter here and now, whatever matter in lives to come, whatever perception of matter here and now, whatever perception of matter in lives to come, both of these are impermanent.

138
00:14:57,967 --> 00:15:02,992
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever is impermanent, it's not worth delighting in, not worth welcoming, not worth becoming attached to.

139
00:15:03,593 --> 00:15:18,349
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is just the same extension, extension of the same thing we just discussed in the previous one, when you're assuming matter, four great elements, you take that whole fundamental domain that determines the centrality, in which sense matter here acts as saṅkhara.

140
00:15:19,130 --> 00:15:22,531
[SPEAKER_00]: But if somebody fails to see it on that level, you take that aspect.

141
00:15:22,911 --> 00:15:31,114
[SPEAKER_00]: Matter being the saṅkhara of your sensuality, being a determination, being the inseparable from... Sensuality is inseparable from material, as we just said.

142
00:15:31,914 --> 00:15:37,176
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what is the main characteristic of... of determinations in general?

143
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:39,097
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the universal property of them?

144
00:15:40,337 --> 00:15:42,518
[SPEAKER_00]: The property is, it cannot be owned.

145
00:15:42,718 --> 00:15:44,399
[SPEAKER_00]: Determinations have arisen on their own.

146
00:15:44,579 --> 00:15:45,619
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what anicca is.

147
00:15:46,119 --> 00:15:47,680
[SPEAKER_00]: The property is, it's impermanent.

148
00:15:49,205 --> 00:15:51,607
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you can't even conceive it.

149
00:15:53,007 --> 00:15:55,349
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, how could you decide what it's subjected to?

150
00:15:56,529 --> 00:15:59,391
[SPEAKER_00]: You're invisible to it.

151
00:15:59,951 --> 00:16:06,074
[SPEAKER_00]: The determinations, the structural determinations, the presence of matter and so on, they don't see you.

152
00:16:06,274 --> 00:16:07,275
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't exist forever.

153
00:16:09,956 --> 00:16:18,000
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whatever perceptions of matter here and now, whatever perceptions of matter in lives to come, it's the same principle as it is with the centrality.

154
00:16:18,922 --> 00:16:30,486
[SPEAKER_00]: Not just the presently arisen sensuality that's inseparable from the matter, but also the possibility of matter through the possibility of future sensualities.

155
00:16:32,007 --> 00:16:37,429
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whatever perceptions of matter here and now, whatever perceptions of matter in life to come, both of these are impermanent.

156
00:16:38,890 --> 00:16:44,932
[SPEAKER_00]: So, as we said, it's that impossibility to own of the matter that is inseparable from sensuality.

157
00:16:48,642 --> 00:17:02,490
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever cannot be owned, whatever has arisen on its own, whatever it's virtually accidental and... and circumstantial, that is not worth delighting in, it's not worth appropriating it, it's not worth welcoming it, it's not worth becoming attached to.

158
00:17:03,451 --> 00:17:07,953
[SPEAKER_00]: When he practices in this way, having often dwelt like this, his mind develops clarity in his domain.

159
00:17:08,254 --> 00:17:13,577
[SPEAKER_00]: With the clarity, he enters upon the imperturbable now, or he inclines towards it with understanding.

160
00:17:14,177 --> 00:17:19,502
[SPEAKER_00]: On the breakup of the body after death, it is possible that the consciousness involved with this will reach the imperturbable.

161
00:17:20,162 --> 00:17:23,545
[SPEAKER_00]: This because it's declared to be the third way which is suitable for the imperturbable.

162
00:17:25,527 --> 00:17:28,549
[SPEAKER_00]: Furthermore, because a noble disciple reflects thus.

163
00:17:29,410 --> 00:17:32,733
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever sense desires here and now, whatever sense desires in lives to come,

164
00:17:33,304 --> 00:17:52,258
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever perceptions of sense desires here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires in lives to come, whatever matter here and now, whatever matter in lives to come, whatever perceptions of matter here and now, and whatever perceptions of matter in lives to come, and whatever perceptions of imperturbability, all are perceptions.

165
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:01,124
[SPEAKER_00]: Where did... wherever these cease without a reminder, this is peaceful, this is sublime, the domain of nothingness.

166
00:18:02,616 --> 00:18:05,918
[SPEAKER_00]: For one who practices in this way, he is one who often dwells like this.

167
00:18:06,559 --> 00:18:09,200
[SPEAKER_00]: His mind develops clarity in this domain and so on.

168
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:13,763
[SPEAKER_00]: With the clarity, he enters upon the domain of nothingness and he inclines towards understanding, breakup.

169
00:18:14,544 --> 00:18:18,386
[SPEAKER_00]: After death, it's possible that consciousness involved with this will reach the domain of nothingness.

170
00:18:19,727 --> 00:18:26,192
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the perceptions of sense desires, the perceptions of possibilities of sense desire, the perceptions of the

171
00:18:27,034 --> 00:18:32,836
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever these perceptions cease without reminder, which is the nothingness, the absence of perceptions, this is peaceful, this is sublime, that domain.

172
00:18:56,183 --> 00:19:03,187
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, furthermore, because a noble disciple gone to the forest, gone to the root of a tree, or gone to an empty dwelling, reflects thus.

173
00:19:04,007 --> 00:19:07,629
[SPEAKER_00]: This is empty of self, or of what belongs to self.

174
00:19:08,830 --> 00:19:13,152
[SPEAKER_00]: For one who practices in this way, he is the one who often dwells like this.

175
00:19:13,452 --> 00:19:15,453
[SPEAKER_00]: His mind develops clarity in this domain.

176
00:19:18,295 --> 00:19:18,515
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

177
00:19:20,436 --> 00:19:24,218
[SPEAKER_00]: Because a noble disciple has gone to the forest, gone to the root of a tree, gone to an empty dwelling.

178
00:19:24,238 --> 00:19:34,563
[SPEAKER_00]: So, a monk, having gone and become physically secluded from everyone and everything, he reflects thus.

179
00:19:35,984 --> 00:19:37,065
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it's necessary.

180
00:19:37,105 --> 00:19:47,230
[SPEAKER_00]: He can't be with other people and say, this is empty of self, because the mind will say, well, okay, you are empty of self, but the external counterpart of you is not empty of self, or he might not be empty of self.

181
00:19:48,372 --> 00:19:54,974
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the basis for this reflection needs to be physical solitude and it says this is empty of self or what belongs to self.

182
00:19:56,154 --> 00:20:05,797
[SPEAKER_00]: So, again, it's empty of the actually arisen present sense of self or it's empty or and it's also empty of anything that belongs to and might belong to self.

183
00:20:07,358 --> 00:20:07,798
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words,

184
00:20:08,338 --> 00:20:09,639
[SPEAKER_00]: The self is not present.

185
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:19,968
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not implied neither through the presently arisen things that self can own, nor is it implied through the possibility of future arising of things that self can own.

186
00:20:21,089 --> 00:20:25,634
[SPEAKER_00]: And the one who practices in this way, he's the one who dwells like this, and it will develop clarity in this domain.

187
00:20:26,174 --> 00:20:32,660
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why this is listed after these three ways of imperturbable and the nothingness, because it's the same practice.

188
00:20:33,873 --> 00:20:38,277
[SPEAKER_00]: Just in regard to the different... reflecting on different things.

189
00:20:39,297 --> 00:20:42,540
[SPEAKER_00]: So, with clarity, he enters upon the domain of nothingness.

190
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:46,383
[SPEAKER_00]: He inclines towards it with an understanding on the breakup of the body after death.

191
00:20:46,443 --> 00:20:50,847
[SPEAKER_00]: It is possible that the consciousness involved with this will reach the domain of nothingness.

192
00:20:52,047 --> 00:20:55,030
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the second way suitable for the domain of nothingness.

193
00:20:57,205 --> 00:21:06,377
[SPEAKER_00]: Furthermore, because a noble disciple reflects thus, I am not in anything, anywhere, for anyone, and there isn't anything mine, anywhere, for anyone.

194
00:21:07,445 --> 00:21:11,726
[SPEAKER_00]: For one who practices in this way, he's often... he's the one who often dwells like this, and so on.

195
00:21:12,146 --> 00:21:30,590
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this... this is now the extension... this is now the same reflection, just, eh... taking like, eh... like more... more personal approach, or rather pers... approach from... from more personal side, as opposed to sensuality, the inaccessibility of matter, the... the two are inseparable from each other.

196
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:33,271
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you end up overcoming the sensuality to that.

197
00:21:33,651 --> 00:21:37,352
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you... if you approach it differently, or if you take it further,

198
00:21:38,132 --> 00:21:48,859
[SPEAKER_00]: You would see that, even once you have surmounted the central domain, you could see that what's there, what's there left, your experience as a whole, it's not in anything, anywhere, for anyone.

199
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:57,645
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, not just that you cannot own it, but anyone, whoever has a notion of self, cannot own it either, anywhere in the world.

200
00:21:58,146 --> 00:22:04,650
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and there isn't anything mine anywhere, for anyone, nor is there anything anyone's for me, for that matter.

201
00:22:06,055 --> 00:22:08,257
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the third way suitable for the nothingness.

202
00:22:09,138 --> 00:22:33,978
[SPEAKER_00]: Further, Noble Disciple reflects thus, whatever sense desires here and now, whatever sense desires in lives to come, whatever perceptions of sense desires here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires in lives to come, whatever matter here and now, whatever matter in lives to come, whatever perceptions of matter here and now, whatever perception of matter in lives to come, whatever perceptions of imperturbability, and whatever perceptions of the domain of nothingness, all of that is perception.

203
00:22:35,390 --> 00:22:39,933
[SPEAKER_00]: And we mentioned that in other talk, the absence of something is perceived as nothing.

204
00:22:40,434 --> 00:22:41,795
[SPEAKER_00]: So, nothingness is perceived.

205
00:22:44,077 --> 00:22:50,221
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever this ceases without a reminder, this is peaceful, that's sublime, which is a domain of neither perception or no perception.

206
00:22:51,222 --> 00:22:58,387
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the same principle of development of the mind, the same principle of establishment, samādhi and clarity, just taken a note further.

207
00:22:59,789 --> 00:23:02,591
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the one who practices in this way, he often dwells like this.

208
00:23:05,829 --> 00:23:12,652
[SPEAKER_00]: After the Buddha finished this description of these establishments, the Venerable Ānanda said this to the Blessed One.

209
00:23:12,672 --> 00:23:14,052
[SPEAKER_00]: Here Bhante Bhikkhu practices in this way.

210
00:23:14,072 --> 00:23:15,253
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be, and it might not be mine.

211
00:23:15,293 --> 00:23:16,333
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be, and it will not be mine.

212
00:23:34,402 --> 00:23:37,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever there is, whatever exists, that I am abandoning.

213
00:23:39,223 --> 00:23:41,364
[SPEAKER_00]: In this way, he obtains indifference.

214
00:23:42,324 --> 00:23:47,445
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhante, could he be fully extinguished or might not be he fully extinguished?

215
00:23:47,465 --> 00:23:51,306
[SPEAKER_00]: Ānanda, in this case, some bhikkhus might be fully extinguished and some might not be fully extinguished.

216
00:23:51,386 --> 00:23:51,946
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the reason?

217
00:23:51,986 --> 00:23:53,106
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the cause?

218
00:23:53,166 --> 00:23:56,867
[SPEAKER_00]: Why some bhikkhus might not be fully extinguished and some will be fully?

219
00:23:57,855 --> 00:23:59,376
[SPEAKER_00]: Here Ananda Abhikū prays in this way.

220
00:23:59,817 --> 00:24:01,918
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be, and it might not be mine.

221
00:24:02,359 --> 00:24:04,621
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be, and it will not be mine.

222
00:24:04,641 --> 00:24:07,183
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever there is, whatever exists, that I am abandoning.

223
00:24:08,163 --> 00:24:09,665
[SPEAKER_00]: In this way, he obtains indifference.

224
00:24:10,045 --> 00:24:13,308
[SPEAKER_00]: He delights in this indifference, welcomes it, remains attached to it.

225
00:24:14,128 --> 00:24:18,472
[SPEAKER_00]: For one delighting in this indifference, welcoming it, remain attached to it, there is consciousness dependent on it.

226
00:24:20,133 --> 00:24:20,874
[SPEAKER_00]: Assumed by it.

227
00:24:22,055 --> 00:24:24,397
[SPEAKER_00]: Ananda Abhikū with assumption is not fully extinguished.

228
00:24:25,838 --> 00:24:26,358
[SPEAKER_00]: But when there is

229
00:24:27,487 --> 00:24:30,375
[SPEAKER_00]: But where does that assuming be consumed?

230
00:24:31,698 --> 00:24:35,768
[SPEAKER_00]: His assumption, Ānanda, is on the level of the domain of neither perception nor perception.

231
00:24:36,923 --> 00:24:40,385
[SPEAKER_00]: So, surely, this Assuming Bhikkhu assumes the best assumption, then.

232
00:24:40,465 --> 00:24:43,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Indeed, Ananda, this Assuming Bhikkhu assumes the best assumption.

233
00:24:43,967 --> 00:24:45,487
[SPEAKER_00]: This, Ananda, is the best assumption.

234
00:24:45,888 --> 00:24:48,989
[SPEAKER_00]: That is, the domain of neither perception nor non-perception.

235
00:24:50,030 --> 00:25:05,678
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you remember, in the beginning of this talk, when we said the presence of matter is accidental, and you realize that, you realize that this matter that's here, that I'm currently attracted to, say, some sense object, this matter that is here, it could have not been.

236
00:25:07,079 --> 00:25:11,223
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what we mean when we say it's inaccessible to you.

237
00:25:12,384 --> 00:25:13,885
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't even conceive where it came from.

238
00:25:14,005 --> 00:25:15,186
[SPEAKER_00]: You are invisible to it.

239
00:25:15,707 --> 00:25:17,468
[SPEAKER_00]: It's there, but it could have not been.

240
00:25:17,789 --> 00:25:22,213
[SPEAKER_00]: And something that could have not been, you recognize it will not be.

241
00:25:23,347 --> 00:25:26,308
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all that is on the level of the presently arisen thing.

242
00:25:26,609 --> 00:25:29,850
[SPEAKER_00]: And now, you do the same for the possibilities to it.

243
00:25:30,110 --> 00:25:32,311
[SPEAKER_00]: They are also present on the peripheral level.

244
00:25:32,912 --> 00:25:37,974
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, it's not just, oh, this presently arisen matter that is accidental.

245
00:25:38,314 --> 00:25:39,355
[SPEAKER_00]: It could have not arisen.

246
00:25:39,655 --> 00:25:40,635
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not arise.

247
00:25:41,156 --> 00:25:42,937
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you take it further.

248
00:25:42,997 --> 00:25:47,679
[SPEAKER_00]: That which has arisen because of that accidentality, so to speak, cannot be mine.

249
00:25:48,572 --> 00:25:55,238
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means any future things that might arise, that will arise, that could arise, well, they will for sure not arise for me.

250
00:25:56,579 --> 00:26:08,890
[SPEAKER_00]: So, setting your mind up upon such reflection, establishing it in it, means whatever arises, sensual or non-sensual, it's seen as accidental, it's seen as impermanent, it's seen as it cannot be owned, it's seen as anicca.

251
00:26:10,932 --> 00:26:13,434
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, having a reflection, it might not be,

252
00:26:15,288 --> 00:26:16,469
[SPEAKER_00]: And it might not be for me.

253
00:26:16,549 --> 00:26:17,249
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be.

254
00:26:17,289 --> 00:26:18,250
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be mine.

255
00:26:19,190 --> 00:26:26,455
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if there is a sense of it might, in regard to your own sense of control and ownership, means it won't.

256
00:26:27,095 --> 00:26:28,436
[SPEAKER_00]: Means you are not the owner.

257
00:26:29,156 --> 00:26:36,261
[SPEAKER_00]: If there is a possibility of things to not be yours, means you are not really in charge of deciding which things are yours.

258
00:26:37,388 --> 00:26:39,349
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you realize that it might not be.

259
00:26:39,509 --> 00:26:40,770
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be mine.

260
00:26:40,790 --> 00:26:42,071
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, it will not be.

261
00:26:42,431 --> 00:26:43,512
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be mine.

262
00:26:44,212 --> 00:26:45,073
[SPEAKER_00]: It cannot be.

263
00:26:45,113 --> 00:26:46,034
[SPEAKER_00]: It cannot be mine.

264
00:26:46,234 --> 00:26:47,054
[SPEAKER_00]: You could say like that.

265
00:26:47,995 --> 00:26:54,479
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it says, whatever there is, whatever exists, whatever can manifest, whatever I could own through my own ignorance.

266
00:26:54,939 --> 00:26:58,802
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I'm abandoning like this because I see it as impossible to own.

267
00:27:00,223 --> 00:27:02,506
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why he obtains upekka as a result of it.

268
00:27:03,067 --> 00:27:04,148
[SPEAKER_00]: A complete indifference.

269
00:27:04,829 --> 00:27:17,086
[SPEAKER_00]: But, if he doesn't see that indifference as also something that has arisen, a phenomenon that could have not been, pretty much, if he doesn't abandon that too, well, he will remain bound with his assumption of this is mine.

270
00:27:17,887 --> 00:27:22,410
[SPEAKER_00]: But, as the Buddha said, that assumption has basically abandoned the whole world now.

271
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:23,891
[SPEAKER_00]: Abandoned the perception.

272
00:27:24,251 --> 00:27:28,734
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's established upon the... abandoned the perception, abandoned the nothingness.

273
00:27:29,294 --> 00:27:32,236
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's established upon the basis of neither perception or no perception.

274
00:27:32,256 --> 00:27:33,537
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it corresponds to.

275
00:27:33,677 --> 00:27:37,459
[SPEAKER_00]: That way of thinking corresponds to the basis of neither perception or no perception.

276
00:27:38,664 --> 00:27:41,105
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, this, Ananda, is the best type of assumption.

277
00:27:41,225 --> 00:27:42,666
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the best type of upādāna.

278
00:27:43,267 --> 00:27:48,470
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if anybody would hold on to domain of neither perception or perception, they would abandon pretty much everything.

279
00:27:49,030 --> 00:27:49,910
[SPEAKER_00]: Virtually everything.

280
00:27:49,930 --> 00:27:51,191
[SPEAKER_00]: So, very little left to do.

281
00:27:53,572 --> 00:27:56,854
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, here, Ananda, Bhikkhu practices in this way.

282
00:27:57,094 --> 00:27:59,256
[SPEAKER_00]: It might not be, and it might not be mine.

283
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:00,556
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, it will not be.

284
00:28:00,596 --> 00:28:01,517
[SPEAKER_00]: It will not be mine.

285
00:28:02,154 --> 00:28:05,355
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever there is, whatever exists, that I am abandoning.

286
00:28:05,975 --> 00:28:07,595
[SPEAKER_00]: In this way, he obtains indifference.

287
00:28:08,055 --> 00:28:09,235
[SPEAKER_00]: He does not delight in it.

288
00:28:09,896 --> 00:28:10,776
[SPEAKER_00]: He does not welcome it.

289
00:28:10,896 --> 00:28:12,536
[SPEAKER_00]: He does not remain attached to it.

290
00:28:13,296 --> 00:28:21,058
[SPEAKER_00]: For not delighting in... for the one not delighting in indifference, not welcoming, not remaining attached to it, consciousness is not dependent on it, not assumed by it.

291
00:28:22,538 --> 00:28:27,779
[SPEAKER_00]: And there are no assumptions and bhikkhu without any assumption is the one who is fully extinguished.

292
00:28:31,415 --> 00:28:34,396
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the Venerable Ananda summarizes.

293
00:28:34,976 --> 00:28:35,677
[SPEAKER_00]: Wonderful Bhante!

294
00:28:35,737 --> 00:28:36,177
[SPEAKER_00]: Marvelous!

295
00:28:36,677 --> 00:28:41,879
[SPEAKER_00]: Truly, it has been declared by the Blessed One, the means by which there is the crossing of the flood.

296
00:28:42,539 --> 00:28:46,900
[SPEAKER_00]: By one Bhante, which is a noble liberation.

297
00:28:47,780 --> 00:28:49,841
[SPEAKER_00]: Here Ananda, a noble disciple, reflects thus.

298
00:28:50,581 --> 00:28:55,663
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever sense desires here and now, whatever possibilities of sense desires in lives to come,

299
00:28:56,590 --> 00:29:02,632
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever perceptions of sense desi... Whatever possibilities of sense desires, now and in lives to come.

300
00:29:03,444 --> 00:29:30,275
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever perceptions of sense desire here and now, whatever perceptions of sense desires as a possibilities now and in lives to come, whatever matter here and now, whatever matter in the future, whatever perceptions of matter here and now, whatever perceptions of matter in lives to come, whatever perceptions of imperturbability, and whatever perceptions of the domain of nothingness, and whatever perceptions of the domain of neither perception nor perception, this is the personality, this is the extent of personality.

301
00:29:32,148 --> 00:29:37,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Means, this is the extent, as far as the assumption can go, as far as upādāna can reach.

302
00:29:39,049 --> 00:29:45,031
[SPEAKER_00]: You surmount the extent, you have surmounted the basis of appropriation, the basis of upādāna, the basis of personality.

303
00:29:45,471 --> 00:29:54,733
[SPEAKER_00]: Just as I said up there, by surmounting the central domain, you have surmounted the domain upon which greed, ill-will, delusion manifest as a basis.

304
00:29:55,733 --> 00:29:58,673
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you don't stop your greed, aversion, delusion voluntarily.

305
00:29:59,254 --> 00:30:01,054
[SPEAKER_00]: You remove its necessary basis.

306
00:30:01,693 --> 00:30:09,057
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same sense, you can't say, oh, I'm not a person, I'll decide to be a not a person, and I'll decide to extinguish the slightest traces of my personality.

307
00:30:09,577 --> 00:30:24,865
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't do that, but what you can do is surmount the basis of personality, not delighting in it, not assume it, see it as accidentally arisen, impermanent, impossible to own, and there will be the cessation of personality.

308
00:30:26,505 --> 00:30:28,646
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, eh...

309
00:30:30,154 --> 00:30:31,094
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the deathless.

310
00:30:31,234 --> 00:30:33,755
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the liberation of the mind without assumptions.

311
00:30:35,576 --> 00:30:38,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, Ānanda, the way suitable for the imperturbable has been taught by me.

312
00:30:39,198 --> 00:30:41,758
[SPEAKER_00]: The way suitable for the domain of nothingness has been taught.

313
00:30:42,379 --> 00:30:45,740
[SPEAKER_00]: The way suitable for the domain of neither perception nor perception has been taught.

314
00:30:46,060 --> 00:30:49,882
[SPEAKER_00]: By the means of which there is the crossing of the flood, noble liberation has been taught.

315
00:30:50,982 --> 00:30:58,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Ānanda, whatever should be done by the teacher for the welfare of the disciples, compassionate, out of compassion, this has been done by me for you.

316
00:30:59,544 --> 00:31:01,025
[SPEAKER_00]: These Ananda are roots of trees.

317
00:31:01,205 --> 00:31:02,065
[SPEAKER_00]: These are empty dwellings.

318
00:31:02,165 --> 00:31:03,006
[SPEAKER_00]: Meditate Ananda.

319
00:31:03,026 --> 00:31:04,006
[SPEAKER_00]: Do not be negligent.

320
00:31:04,266 --> 00:31:06,367
[SPEAKER_00]: Do not be the one who regrets later.

321
00:31:07,468 --> 00:31:08,668
[SPEAKER_00]: This is our instruction to you.

322
00:31:14,851 --> 00:31:17,732
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that was Majjhima 106.

